 {
  "model": "falcon",
  "repo_id": "tiiuae/Falcon-H1R-7B",
  "fact_id": "integration_means",
  "retrieved_at": "2026-09-30T10:17:01+00:00",
  "source_type": "card",
  "source_url": "https://huggingface.co/tiiuae/Falcon-H1R-7B/raw/a6f74bf181389908efd6970878d7ee2b42f5d417/README.md",
  "llm_cache": "data/raw/llm/falcon/integration_means__v3.json",
  "status": "prose",
  "value": "Usable via Hugging Face `transformers`, `vLLM` or `SGLang`. vLLM and SGLang serve OpenAI-compatible endpoints, with the reasoning parser deepseek_r1 (vLLM) or deepseek-r1 (SGLang). Function calling in vLLM uses `--enable-auto-tool-choice` and `--tool-call-parser hermes`. The model generates think content wrapped in a `<think>...</think>` block, followed by the final response. Recommended sampling: temperature 0.6, top-p 0.95, max new tokens up to 65536.",
  "quote": "Currently to use this model, you can either rely on Hugging Face `transformers`, `vLLM` or `SGLang` library. [...] Model will generate think content wrapped in a `<think>...</think>` block, followed by the final response. [...] We recommend using a **temperature** of **0.6** and **top-p** as **0.95** with max new tokens up to 65536. [...] * For function calling, append `--enable-auto-tool-choice` and `--tool-call-parser hermes` to the vllm serve command. [...]   --reasoning-parser deepseek_r1 [...]   --reasoning-parser deepseek-r1",
  "quotes": [
   "Currently to use this model, you can either rely on Hugging Face `transformers`, `vLLM` or `SGLang` library.",
   "Model will generate think content wrapped in a `<think>...</think>` block, followed by the final response.",
   "We recommend using a **temperature** of **0.6** and **top-p** as **0.95** with max new tokens up to 65536.",
   "* For function calling, append `--enable-auto-tool-choice` and `--tool-call-parser hermes` to the vllm serve command.",
   "  --reasoning-parser deepseek_r1",
   "  --reasoning-parser deepseek-r1"
  ],
